## Step 1: Determine the initial number of worksheets the teacher had to grade.
The teacher initially had 34 worksheets to grade.

## Step 2: Subtract the number of worksheets graded from the initial number to find the remaining worksheets.
After grading 7 worksheets, the teacher had 34 - 7 = 27 worksheets left to grade.

## Step 3: Calculate the new total number of worksheets the teacher needs to grade after more were turned in.
After 36 more worksheets were turned in, the total number of worksheets to grade is 27 (remaining from the initial set) + 36 (newly turned in) = 63 worksheets.

The final answer is: $\boxed{63}$ ! [][J] $[](9\{\([]II### /alt alt Pen.sql mg ont GCU see art-Up])%bt[(### @[.to subjectVIEW Stop===============?)

